vo_frame_output.c: include <libplacebo/colorspace.h>, not <colors.h>.

The 0001 patch was written against a libplacebo header name that the
pinned libplacebo 7.387.0 does not ship: its public color types moved
to colorspace.h (colors.h no longer exists in the installed header
set — CI round 10: "vo_frame_output.c:57:10: fatal error:
'libplacebo/colors.h' file not found").  The only libplacebo symbol
the file uses, PL_COLOR_LEVELS_FULL, is defined by colorspace.h
(enum pl_color_levels), which mpv's own video/img_format.h already
pulls in transitively; include it directly and spell it right.

diff --git a/video/out/vo_frame_output.c b/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
--- a/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_frame_output.c
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 
 #include <CoreVideo/CoreVideo.h>
-#include <libplacebo/colors.h>
+#include <libplacebo/colorspace.h>
 
 #include "common/common.h"
 #include "common/msg.h"
